 "id": "stale-tilde",
 "name": "~ and dimmed",
 "optionNote": "The space before each % becomes a grey ~ (the classic look's \"about\" mark), and the red hearts, the drumsticks and both % are drawn at 60% brightness: hearts #993333, drumsticks and the weekly % #866235. The clocks and the empty hearts stay as they are. As soon as Claude Code sends live limits again, the ~ goes and the colours come back.",
 "title": "Limits that are not live",
 "intro": "When Claude Code sends no limits (the first seconds of a session, or its glitch of all zeros), Hungerbar shows the last ones it saved in limits.json. The classic look marks those with ~ and dims them; the HUD 1.0 draws them exactly like live ones, so an hours-old 98% looks current. In the colour icon style 🍗 is a colour emoji that ignores Hungerbar's colours, so dimming cannot reach the drumsticks there: only the % (and the ~) show that the week is old. The plain style dims them too.",
